{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"8b4349eb-5fd5-4fbb-af96-b04c863c18f4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have a very comprehensive set of notes. Let me also read the REPA paper for ReRAM crossbar specific content and the PIM-DL abstract for more details. Let me also check the STARC paper.\n\nActually, I think I have enough content now to write the answer. Let me organize the evidence and write the answer.\n\nLet me compile the key evidence I have:\n\n**From knowledge_notes:**\n1. DRAM-Based PIM (5960.6) - Core PIM concepts, SK Hynix GDDR6-AiM, Samsung HBM-PIM, bank-level parallelism\n2. PIM for MoE (5776.7) - Duplex architecture, Op/B analysis, xPU+PIM hybrid\n3. PIM for LLM MoE Inference (5050.2) - Ridge Point, batch size trade-offs\n4. 3D NMP for MoE (1466.0) - 3D stacking, Hybrid Bonding, 2D mesh NoC\n5. AiMX PIM Architecture (788.1) - Commercial PIM, ISR instructions, MAC_ABK\n6. KV-Cache Full Offloading (3718.6) - KV cache management, ERAS\n\n**From idea_notes:**\n7. HD-MoE with 3D NMP (537.2) - TP/EP hybrid, LP+BO optimization, dynamic scheduling\n8. Stratum (133.7) - Mono3D DRAM, topic-aware placement, memory tiering\n\n**From paper_secs:**\n9. PIM-MMU (14676.9) - Commercial PIM systems, UPMEM characterization\n10. PIM-DL Abstract (5337.7) - DRAM-PIM for DL, UPMEM + HBM-PIM/AiM\n11. STARC Background (2670.2) - PIM architecture for LLM decoding, sparse attention\n\nNow I need to organize the answer following the L6 chip design level requirements:\n- Mermaid flowchart chip topology (Chiplet interconnect, die-to-die, PIM integration)\n- Evaluation table (process node, die area, power, interconnect protocol, bandwidth, TOPS/W)\n- Each structured example followed by annotations\n\nThe answer should follow the 硬件架构和运行时 priority order:\n方法细节（数据流/架构/运行时调度）→ 实验环境 → 实现(aux) → 是什么？(aux) → 方法对比表\n\nLet me now write the answer file. Given the complexity, I'll write it directly to the output file.\n\nThe topics to cover:\n1. PIM design methodologies (DRAM-PIM, HBM-PIM, 3D NMP, ReRAM crossbar)\n2. For each model load scenario:\n   - MoE: expert weight residency, KV cache, all-to-all communication\n   - DiT: iterative state caching\n   - Multimodal: cross-modal feature access\n   - Video: frame-level feature caching\n3. Near-memory computing to reduce data movement\n4. Multi-operator concurrency support\n5. Chip topology and evaluation\n\nLet me write the full answer now.","signature":"8b4349eb-5fd5-4fbb-af96-b04c863c18f4"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73021,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":28032,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6319ec9d-4e39-437a-9e1d-6f68558f0d09","uuid":"5a1ecd85-3bdc-4399-9984-b9e89d1b4b6f"}
